On May 8, 7:26 am, "3cnf...@gmail.com" <3cnf...@gmail.com> wrote:
> I need help accomplishing a speed run. My character, a dwarvish
> archaeologist, just completed a protection run with all 9 units of
> protection... and then found a *wand of wishing (0:3)*. What's more,
> he got GDSM from a bones pile. WOW.
>
> It's turn 6400 or so. My relevant equipment is:

Turn 6400 is pretty good.  Although 10,000 turns might be too tough,
12,000 turns should be possible, if you play smart.

> 1. armor: AC-13. Have clock of displacement and GDSM. There's a +2
> dwarvish mithril coat in the mines if I want both displacement and
> MC3.

You will probably want the following additional armor:
1) Gauntlets of Power
2) Jumping boots
3) Shield of Reflection

These are important enough to wish for before you start digging for
the castle.

You should also obtain a elvin cloak soon, and prepare to switch to it
when needed.

> 2. uncursed luckstone

You don't need to bless this, regardless of what others say.

> 3. oilskin sack, 1000 gold and a ruby for buying from shops.
> 4. a ID'd, uncursed scroll of charging, but not !ea or !ew. Well, that
> takes care of the "2 blessed scrolls of charging" wish. :)

Excellent!

> 5. a crystall ball and tooled horn, left at Minetown to avoid
> burdening myself.

Keep the horn, you will need it for the castle.  After you get
gauntlets of power, you may want to hang on to the crystal ball for
finding the quest portal, but after that you won't need it.

> 7. Most underwhelmingly, wielding a rusty dwarvish mattock. I only

Ditch it right away, and grab a pickaxe and long sword, for Excalibur
when you reach lvl 5.  Mattocks are quite heavy, and they are two-
handed, so if they get cursed you are in deep trouble.

> know the protection spell, so maybe I shouldn't focus on casting
> spells. Oh, and about 6 unidentified wands that could be price ID'd at
> the general store where I just found the wand.

Engrave ID the wands.

> What techniques would you suggest for such a speed run, and what would
> you wish for? Should I wish up most of an ascension kit and dig for
> the castle's wand of wishing? Should I wish for a magic marker, write

For a true speed run, seven wishes will not be enough, so yes, you
should be planning to race down to the castle and grab the wand.  You
might also want to get crowned ASAP, for the intrinsics. You will
probably want to wish for a ring of teleport control, and after that
you should get teleportitis ASAP.  If you have enough gold, you will
also want to pay the priest for clairvoyance before you start digging
for the castle.

> a bunch of scrolls of earth (cheapest scroll to write) for minotaur
> defense, and use those and the tooled horn to play defensively until

A magic harp is also a cool defense for minotaurs and other nasties.
Playing defensively, like a near-pacifist, is a must for a low-level
character trying to dig for the castle.

